⍝ D-99: under )DISPLAY APL2 a box takes APL2's layout, as GNU APL prints it; the strand (D-76) is the default
🍎> )DISPLAY
⍝ expect: display STRAND
🍎> 'TO' 'KEN'
⍝ expect: 'TO' 'KEN'
🍎> )DISPLAY APL2
⍝ expect: display APL2
🍎> 'TO' 'KEN'
⍝ expect:  TO KEN 
🍎> (2 6) (3 4)
⍝ expect:  2 6  3 4 
🍎> 'A' 'B' 'C' 1 2 3 4
⍝ expect: ABC 1 2 3 4
🍎> 15 'NONE' 29
⍝ expect:  15 NONE 29 
🍎> (4 5 6) 7
⍝ expect:  4 5 6  7 
🍎> ((4 5 6) 7) (2 3)
⍝ expect:   4 5 6  7   2 3 
🍎> 'A' 'AN' ('ANT' 'ANTE')
⍝ expect:  A AN   ANT ANTE  
🍎> ⊂'HI'
⍝ expect:  HI 
🍎> ⊂'HIM' 'HIS'
⍝ expect:   HIM HIS  
🍎> (2 3 4) 5 (⊂7 8 (9 10 11))
⍝ expect:  2 3 4  5   7 8  9 10 11   
🍎> 1 ⍬ 2
⍝ expect:  1   2 
🍎> (1 2) ⍬ (3 4)
⍝ expect:  1 2     3 4 
🍎> 1 0 (2 3) (4 5 6) 0
⍝ expect:  1 0  2 3  4 5 6  0 
🍎> 2 2⍴'AB' 'C' 'DEF' 4
⍝ expect:  AB  C 
⍝ expect:  DEF 4 
🍎> ⍕'TO' 'KEN'
⍝ expect:  TO KEN 
🍎> )DISPLAY STRAND
⍝ expect: display STRAND
🍎> 'TO' 'KEN'
⍝ expect: 'TO' 'KEN'
🍎> )DISPLAY BOXED
⍝ refuse: %syntax-error
